WEBVTT

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.840
Lunch boxes

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.450
Hot!

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.810
That day I learned what lunch boxes are all about.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.150
Pre! Preparation!

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.110
I'm not strong

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.190
But pre! Pre-parade!

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.950
I'll catch you someday!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:42.200
P-re-prepare, p-re-prepare, p-re-prepare, cracking apart

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:48.130
P-re-prepare, p-re-prepare, p-re-prepare

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:54.210
If you're not paying attention, be prepared for a poking attack from my fingers

00:00:54.210 --> 00:01:00.300
I'm little, but I'll squish you; you're as tiny as a flea to me

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.230
What I want is a plastic heart (plus, plus, but it's a minus)

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:13.690
But that's boring; when I'd notice it, I'd have won against you

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.360
Love is something that's bittersweet

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.490
Simple and clear yet complex and strange stuff

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.540
I'm only worrying about things that don't matter

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.420
How does it feel? It feels like that

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.540
You're gentle and sincere yet eccentric

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.590
I pretend to be strong all over and compete against you

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.420
Just by being honest, it's so stimulating and I feel dizzy

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:43.560
I get hurt, I hurt you, in a preparation of pure feelings

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:49.100
In my head, there's always a pre-parade of pure feelings all by myself

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.110
<b>What Lunch Boxes
Are All About</b>

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.530
This is nice once in a while!
<b>What Lunch Boxes
Are All About</b>

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:57.820
This is nice once in a while!

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:04.660
The four of us having lunch together like this.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.300
At least the guys.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.620
And there aren't even four of us.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.380
Besides, where's Kitamura-daisensei, who came up with the idea?

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.520
Sorry for the wait!

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.430
I'm sorry, I had to go pick this up at the student council room.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.020
It wouldn't fit in a locker.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.210
W-What is that?

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.790
Could it be...

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.270
A-A lunch box?

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:30.450
Yes.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.380
And then...

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:45.740
Aren't you quite prevalent today , Dai-sen? Carrying around such a marvellous lunch box...

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:50.180
Hey, Haruta, it's not nice to laugh at someone's lunch box-

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:52.850
A manga lunch box?

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.240
No, a 2D lunch box!

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.130
The inside is just as amazing!

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.670
What is this uproar about?

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.490
Let me see it as well-

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:13.990
Minori!

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.110
What is this?

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.010
Maruo is having a feast!

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.650
What kind of a party is it?

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.740
Whoa, lobsters' antennae are so long.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.700
C-Could this "39" possibly mean...

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:27.370
TL Note: 39 can be read "saku".
Is it "saku" from Yuusaku?

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:28.240
Exactly!

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.540
Yuusaku, this is just your grandmother's lunch box, right?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.800
Huh?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.900
Is this your grandmother's handmade lunch box?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.900
Yes.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.090
My parents went to Guam on a company outing.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:45.830
In the meantime my grandmother came over.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.320
Is this handmade?
In the meantime my grandmother came over.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.520
This quality?
In the meantime my grandmother came over.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:49.010
Then she went all out and made what you see here.
This quality?

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.100
Then she went all out and made what you see here.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.170
She really loves her grandchild.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:58.570
I'm thankful for the thought, but she overdid it.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:03.070
Which means, I thought of having everyone help me.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.010
Huh?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.330
Is it okay to eat it?

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.290
Really?!

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.860
Of course!

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.080
It would be saddening for my grandmother if I had leftovers.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.040
I think the girls prefer this.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.590
I'm digging in!

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.480
What's this?

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.410
It's nice!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.720
It's delicious!

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.960
As expected from Yuusaku's grandmother.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.280
It's good!

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:33.690
This is nice for a dessert!

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:34.920
What's wrong?
This is nice for a dessert!

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:35.280
You should also eat, Takasu.
This is nice for a dessert!

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.770
You should also eat, Takasu.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.100
O-Okay.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.690
T-Then I'll have this fried...

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.290
Taiga?

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:43.840
What's wrong, Aisaka?

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.460
No need to hold back.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:51.290
T-Then I'd like to eat the lobster.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.530
You're amazing!

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:53.780
What's with that nonchalantness of yours?

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.180
Just when I thought you were hesitating,

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.730
you want to eat the centrepiece!

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.930
It has nothing to do with you!

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:01.350
No, but...

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.430
I'm fine with that!

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:04.380
Eat as much as you can!

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.480
It's so good!

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.840
It tastes luxurious!

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:16.340
I'm so so happy!

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:18.310
What about your own lunch box?

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.790
I ate it, of course!

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.230
But the lobster is my dessert!

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:25.070
This lobster is so nice!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.230
It doesn't just look good!

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:30.070
The taste is perfect as well!

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.120
Takasu!

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.930
Can I take a picture of your lunch box with my phone?

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:40.430
I want to show my grandmother what a normal lunch box looks like.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:45.480
Eh, uh, I was busy this morning, so I made a plain one-

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:46.630
It's fine.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.090
Okay!

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:49.230
Thanks, Takasu.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.140
This is...
Thanks, Takasu.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:50.970
Hey, everyone!

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:51.490
As if I'd let them think that I was being serious when making this lunch box...
Hey, everyone!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.390
Eat as much as you like!
As if I'd let them think that I was being serious when making this lunch box...

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.500
The shrimps are stupid.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:54.910
As if I'd let them think that this lunch box is the best I can do!
The shrimps are stupid.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.660
If they weren't so delicious they wouldn't be eaten.
As if I'd let them think that this lunch box is the best I can do!

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:57.720
If they weren't so delicious they wouldn't be eaten.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.590
Crabs are the same.

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:00.940
It's so nice!

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:06.820
That Yuusaku!

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.570
I ate too much before I even realised.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:10.110
K-Kawashima!

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:11.820
Hey...

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:12.750
Huh?

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:13.960
What?

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.460
Is Kitamura's grandmother a cooking teacher,

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.980
or does she run a restaurant of some sort?

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.280
She does, right?

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.960
She's a Pro?

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.170
Right?

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.540
Huh?

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:28.650
I think she's a normal housewife.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.680
A normal housewife?

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.920
Yeah, I think she is.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:38.200
By the way, what's his grandmother's name?

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:40.200
Huh?

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.100
Why do you think I know-

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.380
What is with that face?!

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:45.700
<b>Bin your Cans</b>

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.040
You surprised me!
<b>Bin your Cans</b>

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.420
Ah, I remember it now that I've seen that wicked face of yours.
<b>Bin your Cans</b>

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.110
She's Miyo-chan.
<b>Bin your Cans</b>

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.460
The "mi" from the word "year of the snake", Miyo-chan.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.060
Miyo-chan, huh?

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:07.650
Maybe I should have a look at that "serious lunch box" you made.

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:11.940
Just as I wanted!

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.390
This time it'll be a real match, Miyo-chan!

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:17.310
Hey!

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:19.390
Are you okay?

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.520
Kitamura-kun!

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.700
Let's eat together!

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.640
You're having your grandmother's lunch box today as well, right?

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:31.600
Yeah.

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:35.120
But today I have a normal sized one.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.670
I see.

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:37.170
Not too expensive, effortless enough,

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.330
Let's place the desks side by side and eat.
Not too expensive, effortless enough,

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:42.910
and the right amount to fill a high school student's stomach.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.960
Following the rules, the match will be fair!

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.560
Well then.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:49.980
What's wrong?

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:50.800
Okay!

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:52.980
C'mon, Miyo-chan!

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:54.640
Oh, that's nice, Takasu.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.750
Today you have pork cutlets, huh?

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:58.100
Yeah.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.860
Leftovers from yesterday's tonkatsu.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.440
When I woke up this morning,

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.740
I just added some eggs to the mix. That's all.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:06.920
I see.
I just added some eggs to the mix. That's all.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:07.550
I see.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.240
What will you do now?
I see.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:09.360
Me too!
What will you do now?

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:10.160
Using rule-breaking high-class ingredients again for your cute grandson?
Me too!

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:12.780
Using rule-breaking high-class ingredients again for your cute grandson?

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:16.030
Will it be Caviar-donburi? Or fukahire-donburi?

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:17.350
Huh?

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:21.560
S-Simple this time, eh?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.150
I did say rice balls are fine, but...

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.010
She certainly made them simple.

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:33.000
This is far too simple of a lunch box and it won't be enough for a high school student.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.470
I have won this match- No!

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.360
What's that sparkling on the surface?

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:38.100
Sesame oil?

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:39.470
Which means...!

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:40.830
Wait, that's...!

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.770
It's good!

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:47.500
This is grilled meat!

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.480
Such a nice surprise to have meat in it!

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.930
This seaweed is from Korea, huh?

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.820
These kind of lunch boxes are the best.

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.510
This one has plum!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.950
And this one... yay!

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.330
Decisively tuna-mayo!

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:02.830
This is my favourite!

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.920
The "yay" has appeared, huh?

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:05.950
Huh?

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:08.110
Grilled meat raises his spirits,

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.600
plum is a standard,

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:12.520
and Kitamura's favourite food: tuna-mayo.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.990
A flawless line-up rich with variety.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.990
On the other hand...

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.860
Mild taste of soup stock...

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:24.380
All of it, forever, the same taste.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.100
Ryuuji!

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.320
Thanks for the food.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.550
The pork with egg was nice.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:33.110
Y-Yeah. I see.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:33.630
Oh!

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.890
The rice balls look nice!

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.240
Having rice balls for dinner tonight would be nice too.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:43.660
It was good, but pork for two days in a row is a bit heavy on the stomach.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.420
Y-Yeah.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:49.700
I knew that, but there was pork left over, so...

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:50.630
That's not it.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.260
I was provoked by Miyo-chan...

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.900
...and wanted to include high-class looking fried food.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:01.550
But to follow the rules for a proper high school student's lunch box,

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:04.560
using leftover was necessary.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:11.670
Indeed, I made pork cutlets only to cook the the leftovers with eggs.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:16.300
Housewives have to continuously think about food.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:20.070
I did a bit too much yesterday, but now I'm back to my senses!

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:22.910
Miyo!

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:24.280
You're addressing my grandmother without an honorific?!

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.390
Super Egolo

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:29.460
Lunch box.
Super Egolo

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:31.670
Lunch box.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:33.790
What should I do?

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.230
What should I put in?

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:37.360
Lunch box.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.220
Say, what kind of rice balls are you going to make?

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.980
Salmon is a must, right?

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:44.980
Ah, not seasoned, but normal-

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.300
Argh!

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:47.570
Rice balls?!

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:50.590
As if I can win if I make the same lunch box as Kitamura!

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:51.540
Eh?

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.170
Not for the lunch box, but for dinner.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.340
I'll get to that later!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.540
I had faith in my own housewife abilities.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.120
I took pride in it.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.150
Huh?

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:07.250
But you know, it was still as a high school student.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.800
Even if you are the best among your peers,

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.910
you can't easily win when you join your elders.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.260
TL note: A person who is ignorant of the real world.
I was like a frog in a well,

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:16.810
thrown in the vast sea of adults,

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:19.510
and eaten by a shark called Kitamura Miyo...

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:21.340
Dried bonito is nice too.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:23.570
Hey!

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:24.690
What are you doing?!

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:25.510
Huh?

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.260
What do you mean?

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:31.450
I'm doing the shopping instead, you useless dog.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.690
Instead of?

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:37.010
You've only picked sweets and pudding.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:37.570
What?

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:39.320
I also picked dried bonito, right?

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:40.910
That's for dessert.

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:41.840
Ah, did you know?

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:45.380
If you put soy sauce on pudding, it will taste like melon!

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:47.620
Not only is that really old, but it's also a bit off.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.900
Eh, really?

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:51.990
This is not the time for this.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:54.620
I see!

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:57.340
Something sharks don't have, but frogs do.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:59.240
That is...

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.760
Youth!

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:04.220
Huh?

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.930
Hey, Taiga!

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:10.570
Have you seen Kitamura-kun- eh?

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:11.060
Hey!

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:13.540
Five millimetre under the specified line.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.780
Any more or any less won't do!

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:16.400
Just a little longer!

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:17.200
Just a little longer and it's done!

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.500
Shut up!

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.200
You usually tell me not to eat something like this.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:21.890
What's that?

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:23.520
Cup ramen?

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.840
Oh, Minorin.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.890
You even prepared a pot!

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.050
Isn't that great!

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.680
You two -dum dum du-dum- don't hate!

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:33.690
What is it?

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:35.690
You're having cup ramen for lunch?

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.150
How nice.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.040
I'm tired of cold lunch boxes.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.000
That's a nice smell!

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:41.630
How nice!

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:42.540
Looks good!

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.660
Eating them at home is normal,

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.800
but eating one in a classroom is novel.

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:50.940
I'll make every lunchtime a bit more fun.

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:54.310
Kitamura's grandmother doesn't have this sense of youth.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:57.450
Today's victory is mine.

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.650
You won't eat with us, Minorin?

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:04.530
Ah, I have the regular club meeting at lunchtime today.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:06.920
Hey, hey!

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:08.130
Kitamura-man!

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:10.520
Let's go already, man!

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:11.640
Sorry, sorry.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.330
Y-Yo, Kitamura.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:18.870
I accidentally overslept, so I have cup ramen today.

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:19.480
Eh?

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:21.260
You have hot water?

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:22.670
Y-Yeah.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:25.590
Can you share some, in that case?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.300
Thanks.

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:32.180
My grandmother made me take cup soup with me.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:34.420
She told me there are kids who eat cup ramen at school,

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:36.980
so I should get some hot water from them.

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:40.910
I didn't think people actually would, but your timing is great.

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:42.970
Y-Yeah.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:45.210
Today I'm having this and sandwiches.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:47.760
Good for eating during a meeting.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.240
Kitamura-kun!

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:50.990
Sorry for the wait, Kushieda!

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:51.870
Let's go!

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.440
See you later, Taiga.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:55.890
Yeah...

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.390
Sandwiches are nice as well.

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:02.680
Don't eat then.

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:03.690
Huh?

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.110
I mean, you can't eat!

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:06.720
Here!

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:08.670
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:09.980
You can't have it!

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:10.610
What are they doing?
You can't have it!

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:11.720
You can't eat it!
What are they doing?

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:14.070
What nonsense is that?!

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:14.560
You won't get enough calcium if you only eat cup ramen.
What nonsense is that?!

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:18.220
You won't get enough calcium if you only eat cup ramen.

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:19.480
Too hot!

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:25.670
Here you go!

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.360
Sorry for the wait.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.320
It's not much.

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:32.870
It's not much at all.

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:36.210
I pretend that, and...

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.170
This plate has a lot!

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:41.730
Thanks, Minori!

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.360
I don't need your gratitude.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.310
If it isn't enough, don't hesitate to ask for more.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:47.540
I'll add even more.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:49.630
A bunch more.

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:58.140
But still, taking in carbohydrates immediately after school is over...

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:01.810
Cup ramen isn't enough to fill my stomach.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:04.530
And I didn't even eat that.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:07.900
It's not like it matters.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:11.760
I'm fine with Ryuuji's normal lunch boxes.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:15.910
He's been strange and thinking too much lately.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.250
Oh, Taiga!

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.770
What a pitiable girl you are!

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:25.590
You've become unable to live without Takasu Ryuuji feeding you, haven't you?!

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:26.980
Huh?!

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.480
There, there.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:30.300
Food is the foundation of everything.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.630
You have to be fed.

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:33.350
Well then!

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.550
Please enjoy!

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.150
A lunch box, huh?

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:49.570
This isn't it.

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:51.530
This isn't it.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.990
This isn't it!

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:56.250
This is not how it is!

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:59.200
What's this for? A party?

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.550
Looks delicious!

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:04.680
I can't eat this much.

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:06.020
Where's Taiga-chan?

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.170
Don't know.

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:11.210
Can I take it to work?

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.250
Yaegashi-san's wife has run away from him.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:15.680
I'm sure he'll be happy with it!

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:17.890
Ryuu-chan's food is really delicious!

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:20.700
I'll be going.

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:29.860
Guess I'll eat too.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:34.000
Nice.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:34.770
It's nice.

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:35.820
What is it?

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.460
If you're there, just come eat.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:43.000
She's probably just sulking over what happened at lunchtime.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.680
As if I care about that.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:50.680
I will make the greatest lunch box in order to defeat Kitamura Miyo.

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:54.170
No matter what I must do.

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:58.280
For example, putting curry sauce inside frozen rice.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:03.940
Or storing sashimi in a cooler box to put it on sushi rice, and call it kaisendon.

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:07.650
Or maybe something gaudy like a Ritz party...

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:11.610
Stop sounding like you enjoy eating food scraps!

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:12.720
More please.

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:13.790
Even more?!

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.110
I mean-

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:17.150
Food scraps?

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:18.500
Leftovers?

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:22.740
I failed with the leftovers by making pork with egg.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:29.580
Which means something totally new must...

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:30.930
I see.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:31.900
That's it.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.020
That's all I still can- Hm?

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:35.470
Are you faking it?

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:38.050
Say whatever you want, Inko-chan.

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:42.500
I-In-Inzaghi.

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:44.020
It doesn't matter at all.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.620
Filippo Inzaghi.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:46.620
Right.
Filippo Inzaghi.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:46.790
Do you know him?
Right.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:47.740
I don't mind having to use a slightly dirty trick.
Do you know him?

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:49.510
I don't mind having to use a slightly dirty trick.

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:52.820
I will... cross the line!

00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:04.720
The Hayabusa bullet train debuted March fifth on the Touhoku Shinkansen line.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:09.040
Leaving their parents and people living in northern- Hm?

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:13.980
This smell...

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:18.170
What's this?

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:27.250
This is... this sound... no, that can't be.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:30.560
There's no way that can be true.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:34.030
But...

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.750
Oh, a rice cooker.

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:43.450
Really?

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:45.040
A rice cooker?

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:45.840
No way.

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:48.260
No wonder I smelled something good.

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:50.810
It really is a nice smell.

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.480
I started to get hungry.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:57.380
So, why did you do this, Takasu-kun?

00:18:57.770 --> 00:18:58.910
Takasu?

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:03.860
Hey, hey, Taka-chan, don't go cooking rice in the classroom.

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:05.740
What a joke!

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:08.950
Wait up, everyone!

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:10.300
You too, Sensei!

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:12.230
How can you know that I did that?

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:13.660
You're always blaming me!

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:17.040
There's no one else who would do something like this.

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:21.370
Yeah, that's right!

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:22.570
I'm the one who did it!

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:23.870
Forgive me, Sensei!

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:24.570
Anything but that!

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:27.070
Just a little, just a little longer and it will be cooked!

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:28.870
Don't do something so cruel!

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:31.120
What?!

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:32.320
What's going on?!

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:35.500
Idiot.

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.670
I'm done for.

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:48.770
Such a waste.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.370
If you just turn the switch on once more,

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:53.200
it will probably work out some how.

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:56.210
Cooking the rice again would ruin the taste.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:58.100
So what?

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:00.070
You're already ruined anyway.

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.440
The taste of autumn.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:10.450
Maitake... Hiratake... Plenty of mushrooms.

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:15.040
I thought I could win by making freshly cooked rice with other ingredients.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.360
That's not a lunch box anymore.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:18.380
I know.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:22.930
I kept talking about rules, and then broke them myself.

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:24.940
I even lost because of that.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.900
Losing or breaking rules or anything aside,

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:30.890
you got carried away and destroyed yourself.

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:32.600
Here.

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:37.900
I already knew I wouldn't be able to eat decently today...

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:43.650
I will give that to you, a stupid dog lost in a dead end of thoughts.

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:45.950
Is this...

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.480
You made this yourself?

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:50.030
Don't make fun of me!

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:53.540
Even I can make something like rice balls if I try.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:57.250
I learned that from you.

00:20:58.540 --> 00:20:59.650
It's hot!

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:01.470
Freshly cooked rice is like a deadly weapon!

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:02.410
Endure it!

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:05.210
If the rice isn't hot, it's difficult to shape.

00:21:05.210 --> 00:21:06.010
Here!

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:09.050
It's hot!

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:13.710
What?

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:16.930
I don't want to give it to someone who doesn't need it.

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:20.480
I-I'll have it! I'm digging in.

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:24.250
How is it?

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:29.780
What's the matter?

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:30.930
You're shaking.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:42.900
Too salty!

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:48.740
TL Note: Dashi: Japanese soup stock made from fish and kelp.
Pouring dashi into it.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:50.640
This will decrease the saltiness.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:52.260
Hurry, hurry!

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:53.750
Wait up.

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:55.780
Let me add honeywort as well.

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:57.620
Here.

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:01.430
I'm digging in!

00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:04.490
You should break it into smaller pieces first.

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:07.370
It's great!

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:08.570
This is good.

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:11.590
The plum pickles accent it.

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:13.510
I'm a genius!

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:15.810
I see.

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:17.510
That's right.

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:19.040
I'm a genius?

00:22:20.970 --> 00:22:21.750
Indeed.

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:25.170
Apart from the first manga lunch box,

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:28.130
no, that one included,

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:32.430
Miyo-chan's lunch boxes were meant to make Kitamura happy.

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:35.640
The rice balls were according to Kitamura's request,

00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:41.310
and the onion soup was because she knew Kitamura had a meeting at lunchtime.

00:22:41.950 --> 00:22:45.090
Everything was for Kitamura.

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:49.240
But still, I...

00:22:54.190 --> 00:22:56.050
Thanks for the food.

00:22:58.130 --> 00:23:00.790
The one who eats my lunch boxes...

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:02.090
...is you.

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:03.540
Huh?

00:23:03.540 --> 00:23:05.590
What are you talking about?

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:08.790
Just by eating a little I got even more hungry.

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:10.820
I want to eat more.

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:12.940
Ah, pork cutlet might be good now!

00:23:12.940 --> 00:23:14.000
Pork cutlets in tea.

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:15.900
Pork cutlet for the third time this week?

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:18.280
Ah, I still have some thin cutlets if you want them.

00:23:18.280 --> 00:23:19.480
That's it!

00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:21.370
Mille-feuille pork cutlet!

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:23.700
Ah, let's recook that rice and the other ingredients as well.

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:25.440
We can have that together with side dishes.

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:27.230
You can't be helped.

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:30.780
You're not going to eat the dashi rice balls?

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:35.590
I'm fine with this.

00:23:35.590 --> 00:23:37.580
I was surprised back then,

00:23:37.990 --> 00:23:39.680
but it's not something that can't be eaten.

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:45.030
Didn't you just say something rude now?

00:23:45.030 --> 00:23:45.730
Eh?

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:47.030
I didn't.

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:48.670
You did.

00:23:48.670 --> 00:23:51.190
That's why you should put cheese between the cutlets.

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:55.060
I learned what lunch boxes are all about.

00:24:04.210 --> 00:24:09.790
A lunch box you make for someone, thinking about that someone while making it...

00:24:39.600 --> 00:24:43.950
It will surely be delicious, no matter what it is.

00:24:57.450 --> 00:25:00.990
With vanilla salt

00:25:00.990 --> 00:25:02.580
vanilla

00:25:03.450 --> 00:25:10.170
If it's just sweet

00:25:10.170 --> 00:25:15.260
Then let's put salt on

00:25:18.260 --> 00:25:21.640
Because I want you to know more about me

00:25:21.640 --> 00:25:25.140
More than anyone else, I want to bare my self

00:25:25.140 --> 00:25:28.520
But I can't do it, I've got nothing for experience

00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:30.150
It's too frustrating

00:25:32.070 --> 00:25:37.610
But a love that's just sweet

00:25:38.990 --> 00:25:44.870
Is slightly different from what I'm seeking

00:25:45.330 --> 00:25:48.870
If I'm told it's white

00:25:48.870 --> 00:25:52.250
I'd say it's black

00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:55.710
I can't be honest

00:25:55.710 --> 00:25:58.180
I say one thing but do another

00:25:59.050 --> 00:26:02.600
If I'm told, "I love you"

00:26:02.600 --> 00:26:06.020
I'd say, "I hate you"

00:26:06.020 --> 00:26:12.020
I'm happy, but what am I saying?

00:26:12.020 --> 00:26:18.570
Like putting salt

00:26:18.570 --> 00:26:23.870
Into sweet vanilla...
